# rendered videos — regenerate with `./video/make.sh`
out/

# generated compositions — regenerate with `ci-video build`. Not in the kit's
# template, but build/ holds a symlink (assets -> ../../assets) and a 19 KB
# generated index.html per format that is rewritten on every kit upgrade.
# The local runner rebuilds it before every check/render, so nothing needs it
# committed.
build/

# playwright auth state
.auth/

node_modules/

# npm install writes this when the toolchain is installed; the project has never
# had one and both make.sh and the workflow use `npm install`, so committing it
# now would quietly change how the video toolchain resolves.
package-lock.json

# Captured screenshots ARE committed — fleet-wide policy, decided 2026-08-05.
#
# The argument for treating them as build output is that a stale screenshot goes
# on looking current after the UI has moved. True, but it assumes everyone can
# re-shoot, and only three of the twelve product videos have a working stage. A
# gitignored shot set means nobody but the stage's author can render the cut at
# all, and eleven of twelve cuts were rendering as "capture pending" slates.
#
# Committed shots make the render reproducible from a clean clone, and a UI
# change lands as a reviewable image diff instead of a silent slate. Re-shoot
# with ./video/make.sh when you move a screen the video covers.
